  {
    "sha": "6459cedcf2a19e3b18b6a4a410173691e9a1a402",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVouz_toAKDY0NTljZWRjZjJhMTllM2IxOGI2YTRhNDEwMTczNjkxZTlhMWE0MDI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T20:40:47Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Viljo Marrandi",
        "email": "30616+vilts@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T20:40:47Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): keep the theme and colour-vision mode as user preferences\n\nThe theme and the colour-vision mode belong to the person at the\nscreen, not the part. They are now kept per user in prefs.json\n(camcraft-prefs/1) beside the recent-files list, read at startup and\nwritten at each pick, so they survive restarts. The project file no\nlonger writes a theme key and opening ignores one, so File > New and\nopening any project (older ones included) leave the look as it is.\nA pick is validated as before but is no longer on the undo history\nand is not an unsaved change. A corrupt or half-known file starts at\nthe defaults with a status note.\n\nPinned by view_prefs (6 tests), the project_roundtrip test\nthe_project_file_never_carries_the_theme_and_an_old_theme_key_is_ignored,\nand prefs_door::{a_pick_survives_new_open_and_a_restart,\na_corrupt_preferences_file_starts_dark_and_says_why,\na_headless_state_keeps_its_picks_in_memory}.\n\nFixes #877\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
